Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:45:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 089/274] TileLang V4.1 cache writers: hardware E2M1 conversion
 for indexed records

Seven comparisons per value made the indexed writer compute-bound (2-4x B12X
at 512-8192 rows). Each lane now converts its four quotients with two
cvt.rn.satfinite.e2m1x2.f32, B12X's instruction in B12X's operand order, through
a header helper; the division stays IEEE.

(cherry picked from commit 52f622e6d75122e0fd792a69da85e07bc2811583)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/cache_writer.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/cache_writer.py
index e49b2faff..e7d2cbc41 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/cache_writer.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/cache_writer.py
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ are skipped):
   first), then 32 E4M3 scales. A group's scale is ``max(amax, 6 * 2^-9) / 6``
   (IEEE division) rounded to E4M3, saturating; the values are divided by its
   decoded value (a rounded reciprocal would move exact E2M1 midpoints off their
-  ties-to-even) and rounded to nearest-even E2M1.
+  ties-to-even) and converted by ``cvt.rn.satfinite.e2m1x2.f32`` (nearest even,
+  saturating), B12X's instruction.
 
 The arithmetic is B12X's ``write_cache`` for ``cache_format="deepseek_v41"``,
 step for step, so the records are the same bytes.
@@ -25,8 +26,6 @@ import tilelang
